From: OpenWrt <noreply@openwrt.org>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip DISASSOC firmware command on STA
 remove

Skipping the MT76_STA_EVENT_DISASSOC firmware MCU command prevents the
WiFi firmware from tearing down the per-WCID routing state, including
the NPU->PPE hardware offload path. This avoids the CDM2 counter stall
on same-BSS STA reconnect.

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1512,16 +1512,9 @@
 		case MT76_STA_EVENT_DISASSOC:
 			for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(msta_link->twt.flow); i++)
 				mt7996_mac_twt_teardown_flow(dev, link,
 							     msta_link, i);
 
-			if (!sta->mlo)
-				mt7996_mcu_add_sta(dev, link_conf, link_sta,
-						   link, msta_link,
-						   CONN_STATE_DISCONNECT, false);
-			else if (sta->mlo && links == BIT(link_id)) /* last link */
-				mt7996_mcu_teardown_mld_sta(dev, link,
-							    msta_link);
 			msta_link->wcid.sta_disabled = 1;
 			msta_link->wcid.sta = 0;
 			links = links & ~BIT(link_id);
 			break;
